  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "ML-C96-eluppam",
      "sequence": 3410,
      "title": "എളുപ്പം (eḷuppaṁ) — easy",
      "headword": "എളുപ്പം",
      "romanization": "eḷuppaṁ",
      "gloss": "easy — said of a thing, in a frame you have been using for most of the book",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:9c5b2b052ea62a5e",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say this. Then say the little word that finishes a sentence by saying something is so."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "എളുപ്പം — eḷuppaṁ — easy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇത് എളുപ്പമാണ്. — itŭ eḷuppamāṇŭ — \"This is easy.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word ends in ം, and you have been told before that a word ending that way says in advance how it will behave. Here is another thing it says."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Put ആണ് after it and the two run together:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "എളുപ്പം (eḷuppaṁ) + ആണ് becomes എളുപ്പമാണ്."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Nothing happens to the sound. That ം is already the sound m, and here it stays exactly that. Only the writing moves: the m now has a vowel sitting after it, and the bare ം cannot carry one, so it is written with the full letter മ instead."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is not what every ending does to it. You have watched the ം give way twice already — it goes to ത്ത when the in ending arrives, and to വും when the and ending does. ആണ് is the one that leaves it standing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So the thing to carry away is not a rule about vowels. It is that each ending does its own thing to a word ending in ം, and this one does the least."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say the two words one after the other, quickly. You will not hear anything change — which is why you have been doing this for most of the book without noticing:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 3,
              "utterances": [
                "സുഖമാണ്, (I am) well.",
                "ഇഷ്ടമാണ്, (I) like it.",
                "മോശമാണ്, (it) is bad."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Every one of those is a word ending in ം with ആണ് welded on."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You were shown this once, at മോശം. Here it is again — and this time it is not a fact about one word you were given. It is something you do, to a word you met a minute ago."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "eḷuppaṁ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *eḷuppaṁ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "eḷuppamāṇŭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *eḷuppamāṇŭ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "itŭ eḷuppamāṇŭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *itŭ eḷuppamāṇŭ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "LOOK",
              "instruction": "at സുഖമാണ് and എളുപ്പമാണ്, and find the part that is the same",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU LOOK: at **സുഖമാണ്** and **എളുപ്പമാണ്**, and find the part that is the same]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is easy? (എളുപ്പം (eḷuppaṁ).) What happens to its ം when ആണ് arrives? (It gets written as മ, and the sound does not change.) Do other endings treat it the same way? (No — they replace it.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ML-C96-prayaasam",
      "sequence": 3420,
      "title": "പ്രയാസം (prayāsaṁ) — difficult",
      "headword": "പ്രയാസം",
      "romanization": "prayāsaṁ",
      "gloss": "difficult — the other half of the pair, built in exactly the same frame",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:5000578f4e80b5f9",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say this is easy. All of it, in one breath."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പ്രയാസം — prayāsaṁ — difficult."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇത് പ്രയാസമാണ്. — itŭ prayāsamāṇŭ — \"This is difficult.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It ends in ം as well, so it behaves the way the last one did, and you did not have to be told a second time."
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "ഇത് എളുപ്പമാണ്, this is easy.",
                "ഇത് പ്രയാസമാണ്, this is difficult."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One word apart, and the sentence is the opposite. Everything around it holds still."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is a pair you can say about anything you can point at — a word, a letter, a road, a lesson. It is also the first thing most learners want to say about the language itself, and you can now say it in the language, which is a better place to complain from."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "prayāsaṁ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *prayāsaṁ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "itŭ prayāsamāṇŭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *itŭ prayāsamāṇŭ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the two sentences one after the other, and hear where they part",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the two sentences one after the other, and hear where they part]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Easy and difficult? (എളുപ്പം (eḷuppaṁ), പ്രയാസം (prayāsaṁ).) Did the second one need a new rule? (No — it ends the same way, so it behaves the same way.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ML-R96-ease-recall",
      "sequence": 3430,
      "title": "(easy, difficult) (eḷuppavuṁ prayāsavuṁ enna ōrmma) — from cold",
      "headword": "(easy, difficult)",
      "romanization": "eḷuppavuṁ prayāsavuṁ enna ōrmma",
      "gloss": "cold retrieval of the pair, and of a welding that was already in the mouth before it was ever a rule",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:9c7cc3b2fea8eb86",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Close the lessons before this one. Say this is easy, then say the opposite."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: the welding was already yours",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "ഇത് എളുപ്പമാണ്, this is easy.",
                "ഇത് പ്രയാസമാണ്, this is difficult."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two new words, and no new grammar at all. Both end in ം, and a word ending in ം welds onto ആണ്: the m sound stays exactly where it was, and only its spelling moves — it is written മ, because the bare sign cannot carry the vowel that now sits after it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആണ് is the gentle one. The in ending replaces that ം with ത്ത, the and ending replaces it with വും; this one leaves the m where it is."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You were doing it long before this chapter:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 3,
              "utterances": [
                "സുഖമാണ്, well.",
                "ഇഷ്ടമാണ്, liked.",
                "മോശമാണ്, bad."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It was named once, at മോശം, and it never had to become a rule you carried, because you had no word of your own to put through it. Now you have two, and the pattern stops being a fact about somebody else's word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A judgement you can make about anything you can point at."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is worth noticing what the chapter did not need. No new arrangement, no new ending, no exception. Two words, dropped into a frame that was already running. That is what most of this stage looks like now: the language was built first and the vocabulary arrives into it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
