              "instruction": "itŭ eḷuppamāṇŭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *itŭ eḷuppamāṇŭ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "itŭ prayāsamāṇŭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *itŭ prayāsamāṇŭ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "one older word that welds the same way",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: one older word that welds the same way]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Easy and difficult? (എളുപ്പം (eḷuppaṁ), പ്രയാസം (prayāsaṁ).) How is the ം written when ആണ് follows? (As മ — the sound stays the same.) Was that new in this chapter? (No — you had been saying it for most of the book.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
